    "result_text": "Done. The build is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe acceptance test creates an owner and then does `GET /api/owners/{id}`, expecting `$.selfLink` to equal `/api/owners/{id}`. Since the GET/POST responses serialize the generated `OwnerDto` (produced from `openapi.yml` via the OpenAPI generator and populated by MapStruct), I added the field in two places:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `selfLink` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that derives it:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"selfLink\",\n       expression = \"java(\\\"/api/owners/\\\" + owner.getId())\")\n   ```\n\nThis keeps the DTO-at-the-edges convention (the responder functions `RespondWithOwner`/`RespondWithOwnerCreated` already map the entity through `OwnerMapper`, so no function-class or YAML changes were needed).\n\nResults: `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsSelfLink` passes, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS` (1 test, 0 failures).",
